---
/**
 * The gallery moved into the news page.
 *
 * Two published posts and nine photographs did not need two nav items between
 * them, and both answer the same question — what the community has been doing.
 * They now share `/blog`, the photographs as their own band below the posts.
 *
 * This route stays as a redirect rather than being deleted. It was in the
 * primary nav and linked from the home page for the whole life of the site, so
 * it is in browser histories and anywhere anyone has pasted it.
 *
 * 301 rather than 302, which is the honest signal for a permanent merge and
 * what hands the page's standing to `/blog`. Worth knowing that browsers cache a
 * 301 hard: if the gallery is ever given its own route again, anyone who visited
 * this one in the meantime keeps being sent to `/blog` until their cache clears.
 *
 * The fragment survives the redirect, so the link lands on the photographs
 * rather than the top of the post list.
 */
export const prerender = false;

return Astro.redirect('/blog#photos', 301);
---
